        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Oligarchy</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 700 BCE – 1797 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Power held by</span><span class="info-stat-val">A small group defined by wealth or birth, which alone holds the councils, magistracies and votes</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Legitimacy from</span><span class="info-stat-val">Property, birth or entry in a closed register, defended as the stake and competence of those with most to lose; the laws were made by and for the few</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How rulers are chosen</span><span class="info-stat-val">Members elect or co-opt one another into councils and short-term offices; property qualifications or hereditary lists such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>’s Golden Book keep others out</span></div>
